{
  "_comment": [
    "Response shapes for collectors/safety.py, used by tests/test_safety.py.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE, same status as fixtures/dexscreener_responses.json: hand-built to",
    "the documented GoPlus and RugCheck schemas, NOT recorded from the live APIs.",
    "The session that wrote the module had no egress to api.gopluslabs.io or",
    "api.rugcheck.xyz. Field names come from the docs; the shapes are unconfirmed.",
    "",
    "Confirm and re-record on first run:",
    "    python -m collectors.safety --probe --chain bnb 0x<token>",
    "    python -m collectors.safety --probe --chain solana <mint>",
    "",
    "This matters more here than for a price feed. A price parsed wrong is a wrong",
    "number; a safety field parsed wrong is a token that passes a filter it should",
    "have failed. The parsers are total and every field defaults to None, so a shape",
    "change degrades to 'unknown' -- which excludes -- rather than to a false pass.",
    "Verify before trusting a green verdict.",
    "",
    "Cases below cover: a clean token, a honeypot, a token whose LP is visible and",
    "wholly unlocked, one where the LP is locked with no stated expiry, a Solana",
    "mint with a live freeze authority, and a deployer flagged for prior honeypots.",
    "",
    "The Solana cases below were added after the first live collector run showed check_sellability unanswerable for 12 of 13 real tokens, all Solana. GoPlus has no is_honeypot off EVM, so the question is answered from the SPL mechanics that actually block a sale: the non_transferable extension and a transfer_hook program. goplus_solana_empty_report is the guard that matters most -- an envelope covering nothing must stay unknown rather than become a pass."
  ],
